WEBVTT

00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:03.770
You don't understand?

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:06.650
Is it really that unusual?

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:12.020
I'll have to tell you about 
the fabulousness of Mamirin sometime.

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:13.040
Okay...

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:17.130
Momotasu, you understand 
the value of this, don't you?

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:22.610
Not really, but you've told me plenty 
of times about how important it is to you.

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:26.170
I brought this today as a protective charm.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:27.710
A charm?

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:28.920
That's right.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:33.420
There's a limitless power hidden 
within this Mamirin key chain.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:34.850
Let me show you.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.760
Miracle-rin-rin!

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:38.930
Lulu-rin-rin!

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:42.810
May you become the perfect performer!

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:44.790
Boing ba-boing boing.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:45.900
Shut up!

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.710
Can't you be a little quieter?

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.280
Kane-san, you should join the conversation.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:52.510
What?

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:54.030
You're too relaxed.

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:56.530
Don't you want to play Okita?

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:59.800
Sorry. You're right.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:01.670
Kaneshiro-san is right.

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:05.960
You're the ones who 
will be representing B-Project.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:42.200
I'm sure you already know, 
but thanks to Matsukura Kenzo-san's kindness,

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:45.420
three members of B-Project 
will get the opportunity

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:47.630
to perform in the play <i>Shinsengumi Ultimate</i>.

00:02:47.630 --> 00:02:51.690
It's a modern-day style historical 
drama based on the Shinsengumi.

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:55.270
All participants will first 
attend a two-day workshop,

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:58.280
and he'll decide who to cast based on that.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:01.940
Naturally, you'll all be aiming to play 
the supporting role of Okita Soji.

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:03.280
Got it?

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:06.800
I'm obviously the one to play Okita!

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:11.640
And the three of you were chosen.

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:16.610
But... I'm surprised you agreed 
to appear in this, Kane-san.

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:18.170
I can do what I want.

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:19.980
That's fine.

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:22.510
Since we have a little more time,

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:25.550
I'm going to watch this week's 
<i>Witch Girl Mamirin</i> again.

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:29.290
You're doing what? You guys 
are awfully relaxed about this.

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:31.580
I've already read the script plenty of times.

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:33.800
Kane-san, you haven't memorized it yet?

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:36.040
That's not what I'm talking about.

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:37.940
It doesn't end with memorizing our lines.

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:41.450
I've already got a grasp of Okita's character.

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:46.450
Really? I suppose the actor, Momotaro-san, 
is cut from a different cloth.

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:49.700
Are you making fun of me?

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.210
Isn't that your name?

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:53.590
I see.

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:55.930
I'm sorry. I must've imagined it.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:00.210
Momotasu, he was mocking you.

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:03.460
Anyway, try not to hold back.

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:08.270
You seem to underestimate us. 
Sorry, but Okita's role is mine.

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:11.480
Let's do our best for the other members, okay?

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:13.350
Leave it to me.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:23.990
Good morn...

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:30.200
The atmosphere is certainly different when

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.280
Matsukura-san's starring in the production.

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:34.680
Hey, B-Pro.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:38.210
Matsukura-san.

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:40.650
Good morning.

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:42.270
Good morning.

00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:48.010
I'm B-Project's A&R, Sumisora Tsubasa.

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:52.390
Tsubasa-chan, huh? That's a cute name.

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:54.640
Oh, um... It's not really...

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:59.950
I'm expecting a lot from 
you boys during this performance.

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:01.110
I hope you'll do your best.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:03.940
Yes, thank you.

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:05.400
Thank you.

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:12.400
He has a different aura about him...

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:17.040
But the scoop on Matsukura-san 
caused quite a stir the other day.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:21.710
I don't think Matsukura-san knows about 
what happened with the paparazzi.

00:05:22.870 --> 00:05:25.600
But he didn't come to see his own son, right?

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:28.260
He may look great on the outside, 
but I'm not sure about what's inside.

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:36.230
Well, just because he's his father doesn't 
mean he'll always put his children first.

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:38.060
Mikado-san?

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:43.230
Being an actor and his abilities as a father 
have nothing to do with each other.

00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:48.430
Oh, excuse me.

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:51.320
I-I'm sorry!

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:54.580
That's Wakaoji Ryunosuke.

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:55.910
You know him?

00:05:55.910 --> 00:05:58.420
Yes. We worked together on a drama once.

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:03.180
He was always by himself. 
He wasn't very cooperative.

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:04.860
He's not as bad as you, though.

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:06.050
What?

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:11.330
In any case, let's do our best 
to get the Okita Soji role.

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:12.550
You're right.

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:17.940
Is something wrong?

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:22.190
I thought I just...

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:30.450
You'll all be practicing for 
the supporting role of Okita Soji.

00:06:30.710 --> 00:06:35.390
In order to produce a more realistic 
performance, the actor who plays Okita

00:06:35.390 --> 00:06:38.460
will be using the hilt of 
the sword Okita Soji is said to have

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:42.330
actually used, Kiku-ichimonji Norimune.

00:06:43.030 --> 00:06:45.250
What? Is that the real thing?

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:50.640
First, we'll warm up 
by practicing some fight scenes.

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:51.880
You.

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:53.720
M-Me?

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:04.530
Hey.

00:07:04.530 --> 00:07:05.480
Yes, sir.

00:07:14.570 --> 00:07:17.680
Despite his appearance, he's not too bad.

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:19.040
You think so?

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:23.870
Watch out!

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:27.540
Momotaro!

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:30.920
Oh, excuse me.

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:32.840
Are you all right?

00:07:33.500 --> 00:07:36.750
Huh? Your name's Momotaro?

00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:37.760
That's right.

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:40.930
Then does that make 
you two a dog and a monkey?

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:41.940
What did you say?

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:44.940
And is she a pheasant?

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:46.940
Ph-Pheasant?

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:49.340
What's with the attitude?

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:53.780
You're quite different 
from the Wakaoji-san I know.

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:55.780
Mika, that's enough.

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:58.100
Onzai-kun, are you hurt?

00:07:58.100 --> 00:07:59.910
No, I'm fine.

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:01.590
Thank you.

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:04.560
Who's the one who brought 
this rotten bamboo sword?

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:11.380
It's gone!

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:13.070
Gone! Gone! Gone! Gone!

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:14.890
Gone! Gone! Gone! Gone!

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:16.400
What's wrong?

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:19.510
My dear Mamirin is gone!

00:08:19.510 --> 00:08:21.890
What? I'll help you look for it.

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:26.360
Mamirin! Ma-Mamirin!

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:26.360
You're not a kid. Don't make 
such a fuss over just a key chain.

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:28.140
Just a key chain?

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:31.010
How dare you say that when you 
don't even understand its value?!

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:32.110
Value?

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:38.240
It's a limited edition "Magical Super Big 
Wave Witch Girl Mamirin in 2010" key chain!

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:43.330
It's a super-duper rare item! 
They're not for sale anymore!

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:46.670
Shut up. I don't care about that.

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:53.340
Kaneshiro-san, did you steal it because you 
were overwhelmed by the draw of Mamirin?

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:56.720
Don't be ridiculous! 
I wouldn't do anything that stupid!

00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:57.780
Are you sure?

00:08:57.780 --> 00:08:59.200
Now, now.

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:01.610
Mika, calm down.

00:09:01.610 --> 00:09:04.100
Let's look for it again.

00:09:08.620 --> 00:09:11.130
We didn't find it.

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:15.220
We searched not just the practice area, 
but the bathroom, the car,

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:18.120
and even the boiler room, 
but we still couldn't find it.

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:21.230
There's no way it would be in the boiler 
room since you didn't even go there.

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:26.750
Momotasu, you're in quite the good mood,
 despite what's happening to me.

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:29.750
What? How is this a good mood?

00:09:30.650 --> 00:09:31.550
Sorry.

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:32.750
You were right?

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:36.510
Are you that happy to be performing 
alongside Matsukura-san?

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:38.760
Let's resume practice.

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:45.770
We'll practice fighting in pairs 
to help decide who will play Okita.

00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:48.020
It's nearly time.

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:51.270
Let's start with you again.

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:52.130
Yes, sir.

00:09:52.130 --> 00:09:54.130
And Onzai-kun. Are you ready?

00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:02.530
<i>What is this feeling?</i>

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:09.530
<i>Could it be?</i>

00:10:18.570 --> 00:10:19.430
Momotasu!

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:19.430
Momotaro!

00:10:21.810 --> 00:10:23.260
What the hell are you doing?

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:28.100
It's his fault for closing 
his eyes during a fight.

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:29.730
No...

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:32.570
He's right.

00:10:35.710 --> 00:10:37.060
Someone help him!

00:10:37.060 --> 00:10:37.850
Got it!

00:10:44.230 --> 00:10:45.660
Are you okay?

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:48.870
Yeah. There's nothing wrong with the bone.

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:50.980
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:10:50.980 --> 00:10:53.480
I need to get back to practice.

00:10:53.480 --> 00:10:54.430
What?

00:10:54.430 --> 00:10:56.110
You should rest for today.

00:10:57.620 --> 00:10:59.130
Matsukura-san.

00:10:59.610 --> 00:11:01.260
But I...

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:04.760
Yeah, I know.

00:11:05.150 --> 00:11:05.970
What?

00:11:10.590 --> 00:11:13.350
When you've been an actor 
for as long as I have,

00:11:13.350 --> 00:11:18.490
you can tell from a single movement 
just how badly someone wants a role.

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:22.180
You and he were completely different.

00:11:22.180 --> 00:11:23.990
Wakaoji Ryunosuke.

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:27.980
Yeah, and your friends.

00:11:28.530 --> 00:11:30.740
I desperately want to play Okita.

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:39.260
Ultimately, the role finds the actor 
whose desire is the strongest.

00:11:39.770 --> 00:11:41.010
The role does?

00:11:42.210 --> 00:11:44.010
That's how it works.

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:51.840
However, I'm hoping to create a totally 
new Okita for <i>Shinsengumi Ultimate</i>.

00:11:52.390 --> 00:11:55.730
I'm searching for good ideas.

00:11:56.230 --> 00:11:58.400
So that's why you held this workshop.

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:02.130
I feel like I've almost got it.

00:12:03.230 --> 00:12:04.060
I...

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:08.660
I... like acting.

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:18.670
I see. I say the same thing 
all the time to my wife and family.

00:12:21.070 --> 00:12:22.920
Even to Korekuni?

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:26.950
Why didn't you come see him 
in the hospital the other day?

00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:35.100
We're both professionals.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:39.210
No matter what happens, 
we have to put work first right now.

00:12:39.730 --> 00:12:41.660
He accepts that, too.

00:12:47.390 --> 00:12:48.450
He's asleep?

00:12:48.980 --> 00:12:50.950
He must be tired from practice.

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:54.220
He was just looking for his key chain.

00:12:54.220 --> 00:12:56.050
That's not true.

00:12:56.480 --> 00:12:57.820
Mamirin...

00:12:57.820 --> 00:12:58.880
See?

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:04.840
Oh, right. Momo-kun, what did you 
discuss with Matsukura-san after that?

00:13:05.620 --> 00:13:07.710
Nothing, really.

00:13:09.190 --> 00:13:11.130
Do you want to go the hospital?

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:13.020
I'm fine.

00:13:16.330 --> 00:13:19.710
So what was the workshop like?

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:22.170
Momotasu did a great job.

00:13:22.170 --> 00:13:25.270
Seriously? Pi-chan, are you 
going to be playing Okita?

00:13:25.270 --> 00:13:27.360
We don't know yet.

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:29.620
Momo, is your injury okay?

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:31.190
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:13:31.190 --> 00:13:33.450
You seem a little tired.

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:35.750
A tired body needs a bath.

00:13:35.750 --> 00:13:36.740
A bath?

00:13:36.740 --> 00:13:38.250
Let's take one together.

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:39.960
I can do it myself.

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:42.750
Oh, no. There's no need 
for restraint when you're injured.

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:43.940
Come on, come on.

00:13:43.940 --> 00:13:46.010
It's not like the bone is broken.

00:13:44.950 --> 00:13:46.010
Onzai.

00:13:47.100 --> 00:13:50.390
Want me to teach you how to fight 
while protecting your injured hand?

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:51.890
Are you sure?

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:53.710
Momotasu, what about your bath?

00:13:53.710 --> 00:13:55.410
I'll take one later.

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:58.890
Very well. Tatsu-dono, 
will you teach me as well?

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:05.610
That's right. The fundamentals 
of holding a sword are in your left hand.

00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:09.200
I see. How about this, then?

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:16.320
Well done, Sekimura. You're already 
applying what I just taught you?

00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:20.050
I can't expect to play Okita 
unless I can manage at least this much.

00:14:20.050 --> 00:14:21.740
Onzai, can you do it?

00:14:23.160 --> 00:14:24.630
Ow...

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:27.180
Does it hurt?

00:14:27.180 --> 00:14:28.140
No.

00:14:28.630 --> 00:14:30.510
I'll buy some cold packs.

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:32.200
I'll go with you.

00:14:37.270 --> 00:14:38.560
Kane-chin?

00:14:40.300 --> 00:14:40.970
What?

00:14:48.630 --> 00:14:50.030
<b>Stiff Shoulders
Bruises
Muscle Pain</b>

00:14:48.630 --> 00:14:50.030
<b>Cooling Pads</b>

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:50.030
Here.

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:53.280
You're back already?

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:56.830
No, Kane-chin gave it to us in the entryway.

00:14:57.470 --> 00:14:58.680
Kane-san?

00:14:58.680 --> 00:14:59.350
Yeah.

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:01.550
Where did he go?

00:15:01.550 --> 00:15:02.420
Who knows?

00:15:06.310 --> 00:15:07.400
Momotasu?

00:15:10.710 --> 00:15:12.160
Kane-san!

00:15:16.950 --> 00:15:18.070
The cold packs...

00:15:18.550 --> 00:15:20.300
I happened to have some in my room.

00:15:20.300 --> 00:15:22.900
And they just happened to be brand new?

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:26.100
I can't have you holding me back.

00:15:26.100 --> 00:15:27.780
I didn't do it for any other reason.

00:15:28.350 --> 00:15:29.410
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:15:30.550 --> 00:15:31.520
Thank you.

00:15:32.570 --> 00:15:33.700
Later.

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:35.440
Where are you going?

00:15:35.440 --> 00:15:36.560
Ramen.

00:15:37.590 --> 00:15:39.120
I'll join you.

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:40.090
Me, too.

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:42.070
What?

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:47.750
<b>Ganjara Ramen</b>

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:46.390
Momotaro, pass the mustard greens.

00:15:46.390 --> 00:15:47.750
Sorry.

00:15:51.910 --> 00:15:52.840
What the hell is that?

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:56.160
Momotasu loves this place's mustard greens.

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:59.980
Excuse me. Could we get more mustard greens?

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:01.360
Got it.

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:06.770
Anyway, what does that 
idiot actor think he's doing?

00:16:07.240 --> 00:16:09.230
It's not his will.

00:16:10.420 --> 00:16:11.530
What does that mean?

00:16:11.960 --> 00:16:12.990
That hilt...

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:16.500
Oh, the one Okita is said to have used.

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:21.250
That hilt is serving as an agent 
of someone who's no longer in this world.

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:23.480
You mean Okita Soji?

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:25.610
That I don't know.

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:30.260
No wonder he seemed different 
from the last time I met him.

00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:33.010
What are you guys talking about?

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:38.180
Kane-san, you don't know? Momotasu has it.

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:39.660
Has what?

00:16:39.660 --> 00:16:41.020
Supernatural perception.

00:16:41.490 --> 00:16:43.020
Supernatural perception!

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:46.020
What are you talking about?

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:49.920
Is my Mamirin the work of spirits, too?

00:16:49.920 --> 00:16:52.870
This is stupid. Quit joking around.

00:16:52.870 --> 00:16:56.500
Huh? Kane-san, are you scared?

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:58.410
O-Of course not!

00:17:00.320 --> 00:17:03.910
But if that's really true...

00:17:06.230 --> 00:17:08.920
Does that mean it thinks 
Momotaro is a nuisance?

00:17:09.430 --> 00:17:11.990
What should we do? 
Should we conduct an exorcism?

00:17:12.750 --> 00:17:15.980
No, let's not make a big deal about it. 
We'll see how it goes.

00:17:17.880 --> 00:17:21.550
I will now announce the results 
of yesterday's workshop.

00:17:22.090 --> 00:17:25.690
Okita will be played by 
Wakaoji Ryunosuke-kun!

00:17:30.630 --> 00:17:32.830
You all did your best,

00:17:32.830 --> 00:17:39.700
but Wakaoji-kun was chosen for his supremely 
concrete portrayal of Okita Soji.

00:17:41.050 --> 00:17:42.330
That's too bad.

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:46.110
Does that mean we'll be 
playing imperial loyalists?

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:46.110
I'd like to move on to training with props.

00:17:46.110 --> 00:17:48.210
We'll start in five minutes, 
so get yourselves ready.

00:17:48.560 --> 00:17:52.210
Your group seems to be in low spirits.

00:17:52.210 --> 00:17:53.580
What?

00:17:53.580 --> 00:17:58.970
It couldn't be helped. 
After all, I'm the true Okita Soji.

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:03.970
<b>Kiku-ichimonji</b>

00:18:05.540 --> 00:18:07.240
State your business!

00:18:07.990 --> 00:18:08.730
Who are you?

00:18:09.040 --> 00:18:10.660
We are the Shinsengumi!

00:18:10.660 --> 00:18:13.480
We will cut down those 
who attack us without mercy!

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:20.930
That must be...

00:18:20.930 --> 00:18:22.450
Do you see something?

00:18:25.690 --> 00:18:27.460
An imperial loyalist.

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:30.530
What? It's not the spirit of Okita Soji?

00:18:30.530 --> 00:18:33.460
He's most likely a man 
who was killed by Okita.

00:18:34.040 --> 00:18:35.700
He's possessing Wakaoji,

00:18:35.700 --> 00:18:39.420
so he can end the lives of those 
who call themselves the Shinsengumi.

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:44.840
So that's it.

00:18:44.840 --> 00:18:46.720
Wakaoji is in danger.

00:18:46.990 --> 00:18:48.220
Wakaoji-kun?

00:18:49.050 --> 00:18:51.760
Hey! Your fight choreography 
is totally wrong!

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:56.860
Guys! Stop Wakaoji!

00:18:57.790 --> 00:18:59.570
Wakaoji, stop!

00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:08.710
What?

00:19:17.230 --> 00:19:18.600
What's going on?

00:19:18.600 --> 00:19:21.630
Momotasu! How can we stop them?

00:19:24.030 --> 00:19:25.260
By defeating them!

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:26.640
Got it!

00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:31.530
<i>The velvet-like air touches my skin</i>

00:19:31.530 --> 00:19:36.440
<i>The stage is a real game and 
the card I grab draws me in</i>

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:41.150
<i>The reverse side of the 
back isn't always the front</i>

00:19:39.550 --> 00:19:41.150
Prepare yourself.

00:19:41.150 --> 00:19:46.120
<i>in this world full of the unexpected</i>

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:55.070
<i>Ah, I must find my "true" self 
Just go on</i>

00:19:51.350 --> 00:19:52.370
Thank you.

00:19:55.070 --> 00:19:55.880
<i>It's magic</i>

00:19:55.880 --> 00:20:00.640
<i>I won't even allow a moment's weakness, 
I can become anything in this fantasy</i>

00:19:58.260 --> 00:19:59.200
Damn it.

00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:01.010
My long-standing grudge...

00:20:00.640 --> 00:20:05.560
<i>Laughing at beasts who hold 
their breath is the JOKER</i>

00:20:05.560 --> 00:20:10.610
<i>This isn't an impulse you 
encounter often in a lifetime</i>

00:20:10.610 --> 00:20:17.980
<i>Bet everything you have 
and draw the next card</i>

00:20:38.150 --> 00:20:41.940
Are you all right? Are you alive?

00:20:42.470 --> 00:20:45.030
Don't worry. We struck them 
with the dull of the sword.

00:20:46.700 --> 00:20:49.310
Huh? What?

00:20:51.540 --> 00:20:53.950
Thank you for earlier. You saved me.

00:20:53.950 --> 00:20:54.810
Sure.

00:20:55.230 --> 00:20:59.180
Anyway, Kane-san, you jumped in 
immediately to help Momotasu.

00:20:59.180 --> 00:21:01.470
You must've been watching him closely.

00:21:01.470 --> 00:21:03.870
What? Not really.

00:21:03.870 --> 00:21:06.270
You brought him cold packs, too.

00:21:06.270 --> 00:21:09.830
Are you sure you don't just pretend not 
to care when you actually like him?

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:11.060
I won't let you take him.

00:21:12.230 --> 00:21:15.830
What are you talking about? 
Don't be so gross!

00:21:16.600 --> 00:21:19.810
By the way, there's one important problem left.

00:21:20.720 --> 00:21:22.090
An important problem?

00:21:22.090 --> 00:21:23.970
The Mamirin key chain!

00:21:24.430 --> 00:21:26.170
That again?

00:21:26.170 --> 00:21:29.150
Do you think it's been possessed 
by the spirit of a Mamirin fan?

00:21:29.150 --> 00:21:30.530
Are you talking about this?

00:21:30.530 --> 00:21:31.220
What?

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:35.100
Mamirin!

00:21:35.340 --> 00:21:37.990
I found it in the dressing room yesterday.

00:21:37.990 --> 00:21:40.260
So it was your fault.

00:21:40.260 --> 00:21:42.760
Kane-san, I'm sorry for doubting you.

00:21:42.760 --> 00:21:45.360
I said I didn't know where it was.

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:50.790
By the way, there's something 
I want to discuss with you three.

00:21:53.240 --> 00:21:56.180
Momo-kun was incredible.

00:21:56.180 --> 00:21:57.870
Really? I wish I could've seen it.

00:21:58.190 --> 00:22:00.590
It's because I helped him 
practice his fighting.

00:22:00.830 --> 00:22:05.060
So who ended up getting Okita's role?

00:22:05.060 --> 00:22:05.970
All of them.

00:22:07.570 --> 00:22:08.330
What?

00:23:52.980 --> 00:23:54.490
How novel.

00:23:54.990 --> 00:24:01.000
<b>Chest BULLET</b>

00:23:55.970 --> 00:23:58.200
Your body temperature runs hot, doesn't it?

00:23:58.200 --> 00:23:59.190
It's addicting.
